            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0069" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/9–646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Saigon</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-06">September 6, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        7—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>364. Announcement made of signature on August 28 of French-Laotian <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> regulation [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >regulating</hi>] provisionally relations between the two states. Similar to
                    French-Cambodian <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> and Laos will have
                    its own government, administration, parliament, army and finances. Also
                    announcement Laotian elections to be held soon for membership of Assembly which
                    will discuss and vote upon constitution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
